msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:258
msgid "Active: Fast Index sends the notifications chosen on the settings screen. Passive: nothing is sent. A post saved while Passive is not queued for later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:260
msgid "Switch to Passive before a bulk import or a large edit, so that hundreds of addresses do not use up Google's daily quota. Your keys and history are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:266
msgid "Only the checked post types are sent, and at least one is required. Every public post type of the site is offered, such as Posts, Pages and the custom post types of other plugins; media attachments are never offered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:267
msgid "Posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:268
msgid "Check another type when its pages should be sent too, for example a custom post type that holds job postings or live videos."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:272
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:655
#: includes/premium/view-settings-rows.php:14
#: view/settings.php:167
msgid "Daily Limit for Old Posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:274
msgid "Sends published posts that Google has never accepted from this site, newest first, in small batches every hour. The limit counts every successful notification of the last 24 hours, new posts included, and can be set from 0 to 10,000. The size of each batch is random, from 0 up to a third of the daily limit, so some hours send nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:276
msgid "0 (off)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:277
msgid "Turn it on after your new posts are sent correctly. Keep the limit low enough to leave room for new posts within Google's daily quota (see the FAQ)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:281
#: view/settings.php:100
msgid "Post Events"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:283
msgid "Publish: a post becomes published. Edit: a post that is already published is saved again. Trash: a published post is moved to the trash or deleted, and Google is told that the address was removed. Changing a published post back to draft or private is not sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:284
msgid "Publish and Edit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:285
msgid "Turn on Edit if changed content should be recrawled. Turn on Trash if removed pages should be reported; Google asks that the address already returns 404 or 410, or has a noindex tag, when you send a removal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:289
#: view/settings.php:121
msgid "Supported Pages Only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:291
msgid "Google supports the Indexing API only for pages with JobPosting data, or with BroadcastEvent data in a VideoObject. Fast Index looks for these types in the saved content of each post (JSON-LD or microdata) and in the job listings of WP Job Manager, without any outside request, and marks the History entries of such pages with \"Eligible for Google Indexing API\". When this option is checked, only those pages go to Google: new, changed, removed, sent by hand or in an old-post batch. Data that a theme or another plugin adds only when the page is shown is not seen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:292
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:304
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:339
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:293
msgid "Check it if your site has job postings or livestreams and you want Google's quota for those pages only. Leave it off if you want every page sent."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to the IndexNow documentation.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:301
#, php-format
msgid "When checked, every notification also goes to IndexNow (api.indexnow.org) in the same scheduled task, and IndexNow shares it with the search engines that take part. IndexNow needs a key that proves the site is yours: Fast Index creates one for each site (32 letters and digits) and answers it at the key file address shown on the settings screen, without writing a file. While no Google key is stored, only IndexNow is used. See %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:302
msgid "the IndexNow documentation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:305
msgid "Turn it on if Bing and the other IndexNow search engines should hear about your changes too. IndexNow accepts every kind of page, not only job postings and livestreams."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:309
#: includes/premium/view-settings-rows.php:67
#: view/settings.php:171
msgid "Exclude Categories"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:311
msgid "A post in at least one checked category is never sent, whether it is new, changed, removed or part of an old-post batch, even if it is also in other categories."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:313
msgid "No category is excluded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:314
msgid "Use it for content you do not want Google to hear about, for example internal or duplicate material."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:318
#: includes/premium/view-settings-rows.php:27
msgid "Search Console Property"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:320
msgid "The Search Console property that the index status checks ask about: a Domain property (sc-domain:example.com) or a URL-prefix property (https://www.example.com/). When the field is empty, Fast Index asks Search Console which properties the service account can read and takes the one that covers the site address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:322
msgid "Found automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:323
msgid "Set it if the site belongs to several properties, or if the automatic choice is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:327
#: includes/premium/view-settings-rows.php:48
msgid "Weekly Email Report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:329
msgid "Once a week WordPress emails a short summary to the administration email address of the site: addresses accepted by Google, refused or not sent, accepted by IndexNow, checked in Search Console and indexed, and the published posts that Google has not accepted yet. The numbers are those of History. The email uses the language of the user who has that address, or the site language, and is sent with the site's own email function, not through an outside service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:331
msgid "On"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:332
msgid "Turn it off if you do not want the email; the link at its end opens this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:336
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:688
#: view/settings.php:188
msgid "Delete data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:338
msgid "Applies when the plugin is deleted from the Plugins screen, not when it is deactivated. Settings, keys and history are removed, on every site of a multisite network. Records kept by Freemius are not touched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:340
msgid "Turn it on only if you are removing Fast Index for good. The key also stays valid in Google Cloud until you delete it there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:346
msgid "Reads the .json key that you downloaded from Google Cloud, checks it and stores it in the database, not in the uploads folder. Each stored key is listed with its email address, key ID and the last answer from Google. A key can be deleted from the list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:348
msgid "No key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:349
msgid "Upload again after you create a new key. Uploading a key for an email address that is already stored replaces the stored key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:375
msgid "Publish: a post is published."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:377
msgid "Edit: a published post is saved again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:379
msgid "Trash: a published post is moved to the trash or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:394
msgid "Active sends notifications to Google. Passive pauses everything; your keys and history are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:396
msgid "Only the checked types are sent. Media attachments are not listed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:398
msgid "How many old posts may be sent per day, in small hourly batches. 0 turns this off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:400
msgid "Publish: a post is published. Edit: a published post is saved again. Trash: a published post is moved to the trash or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:402
msgid "Posts in a checked category are never sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:404
msgid "Off by default: deleting the plugin keeps your settings, keys and history, so a reinstall continues where you left off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:406
msgid "Off by default. When on, each address also goes to api.indexnow.org, which shares it with Bing, Yandex, Naver, Seznam.cz, Yep and other search engines."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:408
msgid "Accepted, refused and indexed addresses of the last seven days, in the language of the recipient. Weeks without any notification send nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:410
msgid "Leave it empty to find it automatically: Fast Index asks Search Console which properties the service account can read and takes the one that covers this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:412
msgid "Off by default. When on, other pages are not sent to Google; IndexNow still gets them when it is on. Fast Index looks for the data in the saved content of each post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:431
msgid "This setting is part of the premium plan, a separate package."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:433
msgid "The free version uses one key, and a new upload replaces it. Backup keys are part of the premium plan, a separate package."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:448
msgid "403: \"Permission denied. Failed to verify the URL ownership\""
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Google's error list.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:451
#, php-format
msgid "Google answers 403 when the service account is not an Owner of the Search Console property that contains the page address (%s). Common reasons: the account was never added, it was added with a lower permission than Owner, the property is for another address (http or https, www or no www, another site), or the Indexing API is not enabled in the project that owns the key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:452
msgid "Google's error list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:454
msgid "In Search Console open the property, go to Settings and Users and permissions, and check that the service account email is listed with the permission Owner. Make sure the property matches your site address exactly (a Domain property covers every address). Then check in Google Cloud that the Web Search Indexing API is enabled for the key's project. After a 403 Fast Index pauses the key for six hours; to retry at once, delete the key on the settings screen and upload it again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:458
msgid "401: Unauthorized, or the key is refused"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:459
msgid "Google did not accept the key. The key may have been deleted or disabled in Google Cloud, the uploaded file may be an older key, or the clock of your server may be far off, because the signed request carries the current time. Any 4xx answer to the request for an access token is treated the same way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:460
msgid "Create a new JSON key (Service accounts, your account, Keys, Add key, Create new key, JSON), upload it on the settings screen (the same email address replaces the stored key) and check that your server time is correct. The key is paused for six hours after a 401; deleting it and uploading it again ends the pause."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:464
msgid "429: Too Many Requests"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Google's quota page.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:467
#, php-format
msgid "The quota of Google is used up. Google's default is 200 publish requests per day for each Google Cloud project (%s). New, changed and removed addresses all count, and all keys of one project share the same quota."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:468
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:473
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:665
msgid "quota page"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Google's quota page.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:472
#, php-format
msgid "Wait for the reset: Fast Index pauses every key until Google resets the daily quota at midnight Pacific Time, and the notifications that could not be sent wait until then. No other key is tried, because Google counts the quota for each project and does not allow extra accounts to get past it; uploading another key does not end the pause. Lower the daily limit for old posts if you use it, and turn Fast Index to Passive during bulk imports. If you need more, ask Google for more quota on the %s; Google notes that quota may increase or decrease based on document quality."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: status text "No answer from Google".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:480
#, php-format
msgid "\"%s\", or a 5xx code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:483
msgid "Your server could not reach Google within 15 seconds (firewall, DNS or a slow connection), Google had a temporary problem, or its answer could not be read. These answers do not pause a key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:484
msgid "Allow outgoing HTTPS requests to oauth2.googleapis.com and indexing.googleapis.com, and try again later. Saving or publishing another post sends a new notification."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: status text "Not sent: OpenSSL is missing".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:490
#, php-format
msgid "A red notice says the PHP OpenSSL extension is not available, or the status \"%s\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:493
msgid "Fast Index signs its requests to Google with OpenSSL. PHP without OpenSSL cannot do that, so nothing can be sent. Each notification appears in History with this status and is not sent later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:494
msgid "Ask your hosting provider to enable the OpenSSL extension for the PHP version your site uses. The system information below shows whether OpenSSL is available. Then save the posts that should reach Google again; if old-post sending is on, the hourly batches also pick up posts that never reached Google."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: status text "Not sent: no service account key", 2: status text "Not sent: every key was paused".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:500
#, php-format
msgid "History shows \"%1$s\" or \"%2$s\""
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: note shown under a waiting notification, 2: largest number of waiting notifications.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:506
#, php-format
msgid "No key is stored on the settings screen, or every stored key is paused: for six hours after Google rejected it (401 or 403), or until midnight Pacific Time after the daily quota was used up (429). Without a key the notification is only recorded. While every key is paused, the notification waits, and History shows \"%1$s\" under it: it is sent when the first key is ready again, or soon after you upload a key. For each address only the newest event waits; at most %2$s notifications wait, for up to three days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:510
msgid "Upload a key on the settings screen. For a paused key, read the entry for its code above. A post that Google has not accepted yet counts as Total Waiting on the History screen: save it again to send it. With the premium plan, the hourly batches of old posts can pick it up too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:514
msgid "Posts are published but nothing appears in History, or it appears much later"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:515
msgid "Fast Index queues each notification as a WordPress scheduled task (WP-Cron), so saving a post never waits for Google. WP-Cron runs when someone visits the site. If wp-config.php sets DISABLE_WP_CRON to true, WordPress does not start it, and the queue only moves when a real cron job calls wp-cron.php. Sites with very few visits can run late too."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: example cron line, 2: example WP-CLI command.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:518
#, php-format
msgid "If you disabled WP-Cron on purpose, set up a real cron job on your server that runs every 5 minutes, for example %1$s or, with WP-CLI, %2$s. Otherwise remove DISABLE_WP_CRON from wp-config.php. The system information below shows whether it is set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:525
msgid "A post is missing from History"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:526
msgid "Fast Index skips a post when Status is Passive, when its post type or the event (Publish, Edit, Trash) is not checked, when it is in a category excluded by the premium plan, when it is password protected, or when it is not published. Nothing is written to History then. While IndexNow is on and no Google key is stored, only IndexNow entries are written, and while Supported Pages Only is checked, pages without JobPosting or BroadcastEvent data get no Google entry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:527
msgid "Check the settings above. Changing a setting does not send earlier saves: after you fix the cause, save the post again to send it. If old-post sending is on, posts that never reached Google are also picked up by the hourly batches."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: message of the Send Old Posts Now screen.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:533
#, php-format
msgid "Old posts are not sent, or the message \"%s\" appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:534
#: includes/premium/view-run.php:29
msgid "There are no posts to send now. Check your settings and the daily limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:536
msgid "The daily limit is 0, Status is Passive, the daily limit was already reached in the last 24 hours (new posts count too), no key is available, or every eligible post was sent. Each batch has a random size, so a run can also be empty by chance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:537
msgid "Check the daily limit and the counters on the History screen (Total Waiting shows how many posts have not been accepted by Google yet). Run the batch again later; it also runs every hour on its own."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: title of the second notice.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:543
#, php-format
msgid "A notice about keys stored in a public folder, or \"%s\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:544
#: includes/class-fast-index-notices.php:243
msgid "Fast Index could not finish moving your service account keys to the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:546
msgid "Version 2.x saved key files in the uploads folder, where anyone who knew the address could download them. Version 3 moves each key into the database and deletes the file. The first notice recommends replacing those keys. The second notice means one file could not be read, found or deleted; it names the file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:547
msgid "Create a new JSON key in Google Cloud, upload it on the settings screen (the same email address replaces the stored key), then delete the old key on the Keys tab of the service account in Google Cloud. If a file could not be deleted, delete it from the uploads folder yourself. Both notices have a link that hides them for good."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:551
msgid "On a multisite network, one site sends and another does not"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:552
msgid "Settings, keys, history and the schedule belong to each site. Network activation sets up every site, but a key uploaded on one site is not shared with the others, and Fast Index has no network admin screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:553
msgid "Open Fast Index on each site and upload a key there. The same key file may be used on several sites. Their notifications then share the quota of the key's Google Cloud project."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: status text "No answer from IndexNow".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:559
#, php-format
msgid "IndexNow answers 403 or 422, or \"%s\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:562
msgid "403: IndexNow could not read the key file at the address shown on the settings screen, or the file did not contain the key. This happens when the request never reaches WordPress, for example with plain permalinks on some servers, or when a cache, firewall or security plugin answers it. 422: an address belongs to another host than the key, for example a page that redirects to another domain. No answer: your server could not reach api.indexnow.org within 15 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:563
msgid "Open the key file address on the settings screen: it must show the key and nothing else. If it shows a page of your site or an error, choose a permalink structure other than Plain under Settings, Permalinks, or let the address through your cache or firewall. Allow outgoing HTTPS requests to api.indexnow.org. Fast Index does not resend these notifications; save the post again to send it again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:567
msgid "IndexNow answers 429"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:568
msgid "IndexNow received too many requests from your site and treats them as possible spam."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:569
msgid "Send fewer addresses at once, and do not send the same addresses again and again. Wait before you send more; Fast Index does not resend these notifications."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:573
msgid "The index status check of the premium plan shows an error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:574
msgid "The check uses the URL Inspection API of Search Console with the same service account key. It needs the Google Search Console API enabled in the Google Cloud project of the key, the service account as a user of the Search Console property (it already is if you added it as an Owner for the Indexing API), and a property that contains the address. Google allows 2,000 checks per day for each property."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:575
msgid "In the Google Cloud console open APIs & Services, Library, search for Google Search Console API and click Enable. In Search Console check Settings, Users and permissions of the property. If the site belongs to several properties, enter the right one under Search Console Property on the settings screen. When the daily checks are used up, wait until the next day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:579
msgid "The settings screen has no option for old posts or excluded categories"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:580
msgid "These options are part of the premium plan, which is a separate package. The free version from WordPress.org does not contain their code, so nothing on the screen is locked: in their place the settings screen shows only their name and a Premium badge that explains what they do. Settings explained says which options belong to the premium plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:581
msgid "Read the Premium box on the settings screen and the FAQ entry about the premium plan. If you bought the plan, install the premium package as that entry describes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:595
msgid "What does Fast Index send to Google?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: notification type "URL_UPDATED", 2: notification type "URL_DELETED", 3: link to Google's privacy policy.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:598
#, php-format
msgid "Only the address (URL) of a post and the kind of notification: %1$s when a post is published or changed, %2$s when it is removed. Titles, content, visitors and your database are not sent. To prove who is asking, Fast Index also sends a signed request that contains the email address and key ID of your service account; the private key itself never leaves your site. The requests go to oauth2.googleapis.com and indexing.googleapis.com. If IndexNow is turned on, the same addresses, the host name of your site and the IndexNow key also go to api.indexnow.org. Your own History keeps the title, address and each answer in your database. See also %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:601
msgid "Google's privacy policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:606
msgid "Will Google index every page I publish right away?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: quoted sentence from Google's documentation, 2: link to Google's documentation.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:609
#, php-format
msgid "No, and Fast Index cannot promise it. Google says: %1$s For other pages, such as ordinary posts or products, Google may accept the notification and answer 200, but its documentation does not promise that the page will be crawled or indexed, or that this happens sooner. A 200 only means that, in Google's words, it \"may try to recrawl this URL soon\". Google also checks every submission for spam and may revoke access for abuse. Keep your sitemap and Search Console as they are. Details: %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:611
msgid "Using the Indexing API"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:616
msgid "How do I know which pages Google supports?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: mark in History "Eligible for Google Indexing API", 2: option name.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:619
#, php-format
msgid "Fast Index looks at the saved content of each post for structured data of the types JobPosting or BroadcastEvent (JSON-LD or microdata), and at the job listings of WP Job Manager, without any outside request. History marks such entries with %1$s. If you check %2$s in the settings, only those pages go to Google; the others still go to IndexNow when it is on. Data that a theme or another plugin adds only when the page is shown, and not in the saved content, is not seen; developers can add it with the fast_index_is_eligible filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:620
#: view/history.php:145
msgid "Eligible for Google Indexing API"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:621
#: view/settings.php:128
msgid "Send to Google only pages with JobPosting or BroadcastEvent data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:626
msgid "Which post types does Fast Index send?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:627
msgid "Fast Index sends published content of the post types checked in the settings; drafts, pending and private posts are not sent. Every public post type of the site can be checked: Posts (checked by default), Pages, and custom post types such as products or job listings. Media attachments are not offered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:631
msgid "What happens when I trash or delete a post?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: notification type "URL_DELETED", 2: link to Google's documentation.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:634
#, php-format
msgid "If Trash is checked in the settings, a published post that is moved to the trash, or deleted without the trash, is reported as %1$s with the address it had before. Deleting it later from the trash sends nothing more. Changing a published post to draft or private is not reported. Google asks that the address returns 404 or 410, or carries a noindex tag, when you send a removal (%2$s)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:636
msgid "Google's documentation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:641
msgid "Can I send posts by hand?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: action name "Notify search engines", 2: most items sent at a time.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:644
#, php-format
msgid "Yes. In the list of posts, pages or another post type that Fast Index sends, hover over a published item and click %1$s, or select up to %2$s items, choose %1$s under Bulk actions and click Apply. Fast Index sends them to Google right away, and to IndexNow when it is on, and shows the result on the same screen; History lists each answer. You need permission to edit each item and the items of other users, as Editors and Administrators have, and Status must be Active. Password-protected items are not sent. Every address counts against Google's daily quota."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:645
#: includes/class-fast-index-manual.php:144
msgid "Notify search engines"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:651
msgid "Can Fast Index send my old posts?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: setting name "Daily Limit for Old Posts", 2: menu entry "Send Old Posts Now".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:654
#, php-format
msgid "Yes. Set a daily limit under %1$s. Every hour Fast Index sends a small random batch of published posts that Google has not accepted yet, newest first, until the daily limit is reached. The limit counts all successful notifications of the last 24 hours. %2$s runs one batch immediately, and History shows how many posts are still waiting. Keep the limit within Google's daily quota."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:656
#: includes/premium/class-fast-index-premium-backlog.php:194
#: includes/premium/view-run.php:14
msgid "Send Old Posts Now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:661
msgid "How many URLs can I send per day?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Google's quota page.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:664
#, php-format
msgid "Google's default is 200 publish requests per day for each Google Cloud project; notifications of both kinds, updated and removed, count (%s). Google says larger usage needs its approval and that quota may increase or decrease based on document quality. Fast Index does not know your quota in advance: when Google answers 429 it pauses every key until the quota resets at midnight Pacific Time, and the notifications that could not be sent wait until then."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:670
msgid "Can I use more than one service account?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Google's quickstart page.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:673
#, php-format
msgid "With the premium plan you can upload backup keys. Fast Index always sends with the main key, the first one in the list. Only when Google rejects it (401 or 403, or the key is refused) is that key paused for six hours and the next key tried. A 429 answer means the daily quota is used up: every key is then paused until the quota resets at midnight Pacific Time, and no other key is tried. Other errors (such as 400, 5xx or no answer) end the attempt without pausing a key. Google counts quota for each project, not for each key, and writes that attempts to abuse the API, including the use of multiple accounts or other means to exceed usage quotas, may result in access being revoked (%s). Ask Google for more quota if you need it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:674
msgid "quickstart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:679
msgid "Where is my service account key stored, and is it safe?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:680
msgid "The key is kept in your WordPress database (an option that is not loaded on every request). It is never written to the uploads folder or any other file, and the screens show only the email address and key ID. Because the service account is an Owner of your Search Console property, treat the key like a password. If it may have leaked, delete the key in Google Cloud and remove the service account from the users of your Search Console property."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:684
msgid "What happens to my data if I deactivate or delete Fast Index?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: setting name "Delete data on uninstall".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:687
#, php-format
msgid "Deactivating removes the scheduled tasks and keeps everything else. Deleting the plugin removes temporary data (queued tasks, caches, locks) and, by default, keeps your settings, keys and history, so a reinstall continues where you left off. If %s was checked before you deleted the plugin, settings, keys and history are removed too, on every site of a network. Records kept by Freemius are not touched, and the key stays valid in Google Cloud until you delete it there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:693
msgid "I am upgrading from version 2.2. What happens to my keys?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:694
msgid "On the first page load after the update, Fast Index reads each key file that version 2.x saved in the uploads folder, checks it, stores it in the database and deletes the file. Your settings and history are kept, and the old ten-minute scheduled task is replaced by an hourly one. Earlier versions kept the files in a folder that anyone could reach, so a notice recommends creating new keys and deleting the old ones in Google Cloud (see Troubleshooting). If a file cannot be moved, a notice names it, and you can upload that key again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:698
msgid "Does Fast Index work on multisite?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:699
msgid "Yes. You can activate it for the whole network or for single sites; sites created later are set up automatically after a network activation. Settings, keys, history and the schedule belong to each site, so upload a key on every site that should send. There is no network admin screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:703
msgid "Does Fast Index work on multilingual sites?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:704
msgid "Fast Index does not read language plugins. It sends the address that WordPress gives for the post that was saved, so a translation that is stored as its own post is sent when that post changes. The service account must be an Owner of a Search Console property that covers the addresses of every language, for example a Domain property. The plugin's own screens follow the language of your site or user profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:708
msgid "Does Fast Index support Bing or IndexNow?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: option name "Also send to IndexNow", 2: address of the key file, 3: link to the IndexNow terms.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:711
#, php-format
msgid "Yes, through IndexNow, which is off by default. Turn it on with %1$s on the settings screen. Fast Index then also sends each address to api.indexnow.org, which shares it with Bing, Yandex, Naver, Seznam.cz, Yep and the other search engines that take part. Unlike the Google Indexing API, IndexNow accepts every kind of page and needs no account: Fast Index creates a key for your site and answers it at %2$s. The request contains the host name of your site, the key, the address of the key file and the changed addresses. History lists the answers in the IndexNow channel. Fast Index does not use the Bing Webmaster API. See %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:712
#: view/settings.php:145
msgid "Also send to IndexNow"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:714
msgid "the IndexNow terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:719
msgid "What does the premium plan add?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:720
msgid "The free version is not limited in time or in the number of notifications. It notifies Google when content of any public post type is published, updated, trashed or deleted, keeps a History of Google's answers and includes Help & FAQ."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: menu entry "Upgrade".
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:724
#, php-format
msgid "The premium plan is a separate package, sold through Freemius. The Premium box on the settings screen compares both versions, and %s in the Fast Index menu shows the plans and prices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:730
msgid "How does the premium plan check whether a page is indexed?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:731
msgid "It asks the URL Inspection API of Google Search Console with the service account key you already use, and shows the answer in the Index Status column of History: Indexed; Crawled, not indexed; Discovered, not indexed; or Unknown to Google, with the date of the last crawl. Each address Google accepted is checked automatically 24 hours after sending, and once more after 72 hours if it was not indexed yet; the Check button checks one address now. A card above History counts the addresses accepted in the last 30 days, the checked ones and the indexed ones. Enable the Google Search Console API in your Google Cloud project first. Google allows 2,000 checks per day for each property; the automatic checks use at most half of them. The address and the property go to searchconsole.googleapis.com."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:735
msgid "How do I get the premium plan, and how do I install it?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: menu entry "Upgrade", 2: button "Upgrade to Premium", 3: link to the Freemius customer portal.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:738
#, php-format
msgid "Open %1$s in the Fast Index menu, or click %2$s on the settings screen, and buy a plan there; Freemius handles the payment. Freemius then emails you the premium package (a .zip file) and a license key; both are also in your account at %3$s. In WordPress go to Plugins, add a new plugin, click Upload Plugin and choose that .zip file, then activate it and enter the license key when you are asked. If both versions are installed, Freemius deactivates the free one. Your settings, keys and history are kept. The free version from WordPress.org never contains the premium code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:740
#: view/settings.php:341
msgid "Upgrade to Premium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:746
msgid "What is Freemius, and do I have to connect an account?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: button "Skip", 2: button "Allow & Continue", 3: link to the Freemius privacy policy.
#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:749
#, php-format
msgid "No. Fast Index includes the Freemius SDK, which sells the premium plan and manages its licenses. The free version has no license screen. The first time you open Fast Index, Freemius shows an opt-in screen. If you choose %1$s, nothing is sent to Freemius and Fast Index works the same. If you choose %2$s, your browser sends what that screen lists to Freemius: your name and email address, the site address and title, the language, the WordPress, PHP, plugin and SDK versions, and later the list of your plugins and themes. Opening Upgrade loads the plans from Freemius without any site data, and choosing a plan opens the Freemius checkout. See %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:752
msgid "the Freemius privacy policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:757
msgid "Does Fast Index slow down saving posts?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:758
msgid "No. Saving a post only queues a scheduled task. The request to Google is made later by WP-Cron, with a time limit of 15 seconds, and a batch of old posts stops after about 20 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:779
msgid "Read the Troubleshooting entry that matches the code in History, and the FAQ."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:780
msgid "On the settings screen, look at the last answer shown next to each key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:781
msgid "In Search Console, check that the service account is an Owner of a property that matches your site address exactly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-fast-index-help-content.php:782
